   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend a chapter of the laws of 2013, relating to authorizing the East Ramapo central school district to receive certain apportionments on an accelerated basis, as proposed in legislative bills numbers S. 5057-A and A. 7514, in relation to the 2013-2014 school year",
    "basePrintNo": "S5939",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S5939-2013",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §2, Chap of 2013 (as proposed in A.7514 and S.5057-A)",
    "lawSection": "Education",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S5939\n\nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend a chapter of the laws of 2013,\nrelating to authorizing the East Ramapo central school district to\nreceive certain apportionments on an accelerated basis, as proposed in\nlegislative bills numbers S. 5057-A and A. 7514, in relation to the\n2013-2014 school year\n\nPURPOSE:\n\nTo clarify that the temporary advisory committee established pursuant\nto a chapter of the laws of 2013 as proposed in legislative bills\nS.5057-A and A.7514 shall remain in effect for only the 13-14 school\nyear.\n\nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nProvides that, for the 13-14 school year, before the expenditure of\nfunds received pursuant to the lottery spin-up the superintendent of\nthe East Ramapo central school district shall appoint a temporary\ndistrict based advisory team in the 13-14 school year to develop a\ncomprehensive expenditure plan of such funds in this first year.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis bill would clarify that the temporary advisory committee will\ndevelop a comprehensive expenditure plan only in the 13-14 school\nyear.\n\nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\n\nThis act shall take effect on the same date and in the same manner as\na chapter of the laws of 2013 relating to authorizing the East Ramapo\ncentral school district to receive certain apportionments on an\naccelerated basis, as proposed in legislative bills S.5057-A and\nA.7514.\n\n",
